EXACT DOMINATION - ALL TEST CASES
=================================
Assumption: intervals are half-open, so back-to-back lectures
(one ends at 10:00, the next starts at 10:00) do NOT overlap.

Input format for each case:
    n
    n lines of "HH:MM HH:MM"  (start end)

Each case below starts with a "### TEST" line. The lines under
"INPUT" are what you give to the program. The line under "EXPECTED"
is the correct output.


### TEST 01: single lecture
INPUT
1
09:00 10:00
EXPECTED
Selected lectures: 1


### TEST 02: one lecture overlaps all the others
INPUT
3
09:00 12:00
09:30 10:30
11:00 11:30
EXPECTED
Selected lectures: 1     (only valid answer)


### TEST 03: identical lectures (all overlap each other)
INPUT
3
09:00 10:00
09:00 10:00
09:00 10:00
EXPECTED
Selected lectures: 1     (2 or 3 is also valid)


### TEST 04: all disjoint (every lecture must be chosen)
INPUT
3
08:00 09:00
10:00 11:00
12:00 13:00
EXPECTED
Selected lectures: 1 2 3


### TEST 05: two separate groups
INPUT
4
08:00 09:00
08:30 09:30
13:00 14:00
13:30 14:30
EXPECTED
Any one of: 1 3 / 1 4 / 2 3 / 2 4


### TEST 06: chain 1-2-3-4 (unique answer)
INPUT
4
08:00 10:00
09:00 11:00
10:00 12:00
11:00 13:00
EXPECTED
Selected lectures: 1 4   (only valid answer)


### TEST 07: touching lectures (edge case)
INPUT
2
08:00 10:00
10:00 12:00
EXPECTED
Selected lectures: 1 2
(If touching counted as overlapping, the answer would be 1 or 2.)


### TEST 08: lectures crossing midnight
INPUT
3
23:00 01:00
00:30 02:00
12:00 13:00
EXPECTED
Any one of: 1 3 / 2 3


### TEST 09: ring of 6 (solution wraps around the whole day)
INPUT
6
00:00 05:00
04:00 09:00
08:00 13:00
12:00 17:00
16:00 21:00
20:00 01:00
EXPECTED
Any one of: 1 4 / 2 5 / 3 6


### TEST 10: ring of 5 (no solution)
INPUT
5
00:00 06:00
05:00 11:00
10:00 16:00
15:00 21:00
20:00 02:00
EXPECTED
No valid subset exists.


### TEST 11: ring of 4 (no solution)
INPUT
4
00:00 07:00
06:00 13:00
12:00 19:00
18:00 01:00
EXPECTED
No valid subset exists.
